\title{Cause-specific and subdistribution hazard ratios}
\description{
Both models are fitted and reported side by side, because they answer different questions and can point in different directions.
}
\details{
The cause-specific hazard ratio asks how much faster the outcome happens among those still at risk; the subdistribution (Fine-Gray) hazard ratio asks how much the cumulative incidence differs. A treatment that prolongs survival grants more time in which to reach the outcome, and only the second reflects that. Neither is called "the" hazard ratio.
}
